  "notes": "First UK pressing. \n\"Pink scroll\" Charisma labels. \nMatte gatefold sleeve. \nPrinted red/white inner sleeve with lyrics. \n \nCatalogue number CAS 1032 credited on labels, rear of sleeve and in parentheses on lyric inner. \n \n[Labels]\n\u2117 1971 \nTracks A1 to B2 & B4. Essex Music\nTrack B3. United Artists Music\n \n[Sleeve] \nThe string arrangement on Raviol\u00e9 by R. Kirby, who conducted members of the L.S.O. \nSleeve design and photography by HIPGNOSIS based on an original screenplay by Hipgnosis and Howard Werth\nB & C Records Ltd., 37 Soho Square, London, W.1.\nPrinted and made by the E. J. Day Group, London and Bedford\n\nAll matrix runouts are stamped.",
